---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const title = 'Refund policy | Madrid';
const description =
  'How refunds work for Madrid (web-billed subscriptions). UK statutory rights are not limited by this policy.';
---

<LegalLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  heading="Refund policy"
  lede="This describes how we handle refunds for Madrid. It is written in plain language and does not replace your statutory rights as a UK consumer where those apply."
  breadcrumb="Refund policy"
  updated="2026-09-05"
>
  <h2>Download only</h2>
  <p>
    You may download the Madrid app for macOS without charge. If you have not completed a paid subscription or one-time
    purchase, there is no payment to refund. Uninstall the app from your Mac if you no longer want it.
  </p>

  <h2>Web billing (subscriptions)</h2>
  <p>
    If you subscribed to Madrid through web billing (checkout powered by Stripe via our subscription provider), you may
    request a refund by contacting us from Settings in the Madrid app after you sign in, or by replying to your purchase
    receipt if one was emailed to you. We aim to respond within a few business days.
  </p>
  <p>
    Approved refunds are processed back to your original payment method where possible. When a subscription payment is
    refunded or you cancel, cloud sync and other paid features may end when the billing period or grace period described
    at checkout no longer applies.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe a charge is incorrect or unauthorised, contact us promptly so we can review it with you and, if
    needed, your card issuer.
  </p>

  <h2>App Store and other storefronts</h2>
  <p>
    If you buy or renew Madrid through the Mac App Store or another platform, refunds and billing support are handled by
    that store under its own rules. Use Apple's support flows, or the relevant store's process, for those purchases;
    this page applies to web-billed subscriptions only.
  </p>

  <h2>UK statutory rights</h2>
  <p>
    If you are in the UK, you may have statutory rights, for example under consumer protection law, in addition to this
    policy. Nothing here is intended to limit those rights. For legal certainty about your situation, consider
    independent advice.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
